Part III: Administration

- The Director General supervises sales tax matters, with the Minister providing overall direction.

- Officers of sales tax with proper authorization may perform duties related to sales tax enforcement.

- You, as an officer, must be recognized as a public servant under the Penal Code.

- You are required to submit audit certificates if registered.

- You must notify the Director General if your company is liquidated.

Part IV: Review and Appeal

- You may appeal the Director General's decision regarding your registration or tax assessment within thirty days if no further appeal is made.

